CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ pack expansion: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
static assertion failed
--
The static assertions are checked at compile time; a wrong evaluation
reports "static assertion failed" and a CONVERSION ERROR.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
